# What the verification suites leave behind. They take an output directory as
# an argument and default to the repository root, so a run started without one
# drops its screenshots here. Ignored rather than forbidden: the screenshots
# are genuinely useful while you are looking at them, and worthless afterwards.
/*.png
/exported.csv
/shots/
# A run once received a URL where it expected an output directory, and made a
# folder literally called `http:`. Ignored so the same slip cannot commit one.
/http:/

